<speak>Not usually. The difficulty is finding a quiet moment, not opening it. On supplier visits there is always somebody walking beside me, or a car arriving, or a discussion continuing over lunch. I do not like reading private correspondence with people looking over my shoulder. I tend to leave it until I am back at the hotel. By then, the office has sent a collection of messages of its own, and I have to work out which ones genuinely need an answer. I am trying to separate things I must decide from things people merely want me to see.</speak>